# Release-related files need a releaser. The last matching pattern wins.
#
# No default owner for now, so that authors can merge their own PRs while
# development settles (GitHub never counts the author's own approval, even when
# they are in @topotal/all). Release PRs are opened by the tagpr bot, so a
# releaser can still approve them. Restore the line below once development is
# stable or outside contributions start, to require a review on every PR.
# *                             @topotal/all

# Only the tagpr release PR changes the version file, so release PRs need a releaser.
/waroom/sdk_version.go          @topotal/waroom-ecosystem-releasers

# Release pipeline: tagging and GoReleaser.
/.tagpr                         @topotal/waroom-ecosystem-releasers
/.goreleaser.yaml               @topotal/waroom-ecosystem-releasers

# Everything under .github/: workflows, local actions, and this file. Any workflow
# on main can declare `environment: release` and read the App key, so every
# workflow change needs a releaser, not just release.yaml and sync-openapi.yaml.
/.github/                       @topotal/waroom-ecosystem-releasers
